    "accordion_X9KDBB": {
      "type": "accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "text_8HeDjV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Miami's water quality safe?",
            "answer": "<p>The water quality in Miami is at or above the minimum federal level required by law; however, Miami's water may contain pollutants such as microplastics, lead, and disinfection byproducts. Due to local conditions and old infrastructure, additional filtration is often suggested.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_QbTBtT": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What contaminants does Phoenix Gravity remove from Miami tap water?",
            "answer": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Water Filters eliminate 99.9% of all local pollutants, such as lead, microplastics, PFASs, and byproducts of disinfection (TTHMs/ HAA5). It also provides efficient filtration for industrial runoff or the nitrates of the Miami water quality report.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_XbcVQV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Phoenix Gravity ship to Miami and South Florida?",
            "answer": "<p>Of course! Phoenix Gravity provides free shipping to Miami and all of South Florida. We ship out quickly, so you will have great-tasting, clean drinking water ASAP.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_NXHddK": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What warranty and guarantee come with the Phoenix Gravity filter?",
            "answer": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Filter is covered by a 10-year warranty, and if, for any reason, you decide you don't like the water, you can return it within 100 days.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_yUeHba": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How often do I need to replace the Carbon filter elements?",
            "answer": "<p>One pair of Phoenix Gravity Carbon filter elements is good for up to 5,500 gallons of water. So for most homes in Miami, you will be enjoying many years of fresh water at a price of less than 5 cents per gallon.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_fE9Y4D": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need a plumber or any installation for Phoenix Gravity Filters?",
            "answer": "<p>There is no need for a plumber because of the tool-free gravity design of the system; there is no installation required and no power needed. The system offers the easiest solution to keep your Miami tap water safe from lead and microplastics and provide you with clean drinking water.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_XzRedf": {
          "type": "text",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is chloramine used in New York water?",
            "answer": "<p>The main reason chloramines are added to NY water is because they provide protection for the water by serving as a disinfectant while being transported through pipes to customers. Chloramines can leave a particular flavor in the water therefore, they may need to be filtered to improve their quality. </p>"
          }
        },
        "text_bVMT6E": {
          "type": "text",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is chromium 6 in New York water and should I worry?",
            "answer": "<p>Chromium (VI) is a toxic heavy metal that is found in trace amounts in NY water and is associated with industrial pollution. The greatest worry is for long-term exposure; therefore, any kind of effective filtration is very important. </p>"
          }
        }
      },
